WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:04.500
Chapter 18 of "The Mandalorian" features&nbsp;
Din Djarin using the Darksaber once again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.440
but he still hasn't fully mastered&nbsp;
the strange weapon. But his failure&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:10.140
to wield it competently is more&nbsp;
complicated than you might think.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.200
The idea of a black lightsaber sure&nbsp;
sounds like something that would live&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.380
in a teenage "Star Wars" fan's&nbsp;
sketchbook. And yet, it's canon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:20.280
and becoming ever more important to the&nbsp;
franchise. Since being introduced in "Star Wars:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.280 --> 00:00:24.300
The Clone Wars," the Darksaber has popped up&nbsp;
in both "Rebels" and "The Mandalorian." It's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.720
an ancient weapon with a rich history&nbsp;
tied to both the Jedi and Mandalore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:32.100
and now it rests safely in the capable hands&nbsp;
of Din Djarin. Or, well, mostly capable.

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:36.180
Despite training intensely with the blade in&nbsp;
"The Book of Boba Fett," Din still struggles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:40.380
with it in "The Mandalorian" Chapter 18. His form&nbsp;
is awkward, and he seems to be fighting against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:44.940
the Darksaber as much as he's fighting with it.&nbsp;
The Darksaber was forged by an ancient Mandalorian&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:49.260
Jedi named Tarre Vizsla. After his death, it&nbsp;
was stolen from the Jedi Temple by his clan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:52.980
and since then, it's been passed down.&nbsp;
Traditionally, the weapon is won in combat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.580
but earning it doesn't guarantee you'll&nbsp;
be able to wield it, as Din finds out.

00:00:56.580 --> 00:01:01.320
Like all lightsabers, the Darksaber is designed&nbsp;
to tightly focus energy from the crystal at its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.320 --> 00:01:05.660
core. Kanan Jarrus gives Sabine Wren some&nbsp;
very useful advice in "Star Wars Rebels."

00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:09.746
"You're not fighting with a simple blade as&nbsp;
much as you are directing a current of power."

00:01:09.746 --> 00:01:14.400
Like Din, Sabine struggles at first to control&nbsp;
the energy of the blade. Kanan blames this on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:18.120
her inner turmoil, saying that her thoughts and&nbsp;
feelings are also channeled through the weapon.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:21.540
When she begins to master it, he says that&nbsp;
it's because she's connecting to the blade.

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:24.660
The Armorer tells Din something similar&nbsp;
in "The Book of Boba Fett" when he's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.660
training with the Darksaber. He says&nbsp;
that each swing makes it heavier,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.660 --> 00:01:30.840
and she says it's because he's "fighting&nbsp;
against the blade." According to her,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:35.580
his lack of dexterity is the result of a lack of&nbsp;
focus. In other words, Din has a mental block when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:39.960
it comes to the Darksaber, which is clearly&nbsp;
still in place in "The Mandalorian" Season 3.

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:44.040
Perhaps he's too concerned with redeeming himself&nbsp;
in the eyes of his people. Or maybe it's his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.040 --> 00:01:48.591
paternal feelings for Grogu that are throwing him&nbsp;
off. Whatever the cause, the effects are clear.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.591 --> 00:01:53.460
Still, there is hope. Just as Sabine, Pre Vizsla,&nbsp;
and Bo-Katan all came to master the Darksaber,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.460 --> 00:01:57.900
so too can Din. The main issue is probably just&nbsp;
that his priorities are elsewhere at the moment.

00:01:57.900 --> 00:02:02.040
Why is the Darksaber so much more challenging&nbsp;
to master than a regular lightsaber? Well,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:06.180
for starters, that might not actually be true.&nbsp;
Most of the lightsaber training we've seen in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.180 --> 00:02:10.020
"Star Wars" involves Force-sensitive characters,&nbsp;
who have a natural advantage in wielding the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.020 --> 00:02:13.920
iconic weapons. The Darksaber is more often&nbsp;
used by Mandalorians who have no natural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:18.095
Force power. As such, they have to adapt to a&nbsp;
tool that was not designed with them in mind.

00:02:18.095 --> 00:02:22.020
Even still, the Darksaber seems more&nbsp;
challenging to control. Jedi younglings&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:26.100
have better dexterity with their blades than&nbsp;
Din, and there are numerous instances across&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:29.460
the franchise of lightsabers being used&nbsp;
by characters who aren't Force-sensitive.

00:02:29.460 --> 00:02:34.560
Why is the Darksaber in particular so difficult?&nbsp;
There are a few possible explanations. For one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.560 --> 00:02:37.860
it's a much older design than the other&nbsp;
lightsabers we see in "Star Wars," so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.100
it's possible that its energy is less&nbsp;
restrained. There's precedent for this,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:43.860
as Kylo Ren's lightsaber also uses unstable power&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.860 --> 00:02:47.400
to yield a more forceful weapon. The&nbsp;
Darksaber is also a fully unique model,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.046
so there could be some secret Mandalorian&nbsp;
features that make it different to wield.

00:02:51.046 --> 00:02:54.600
It's hard to say for sure because we've never&nbsp;
seen a character who isn't Force-sensitive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:54.600 --> 00:02:58.351
train this much with a regular lightsaber.&nbsp;
When Kanan instructs Sabine in "Rebels,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.351 --> 00:03:01.920
he seems to know what she's experiencing with&nbsp;
the Darksaber despite not being familiar with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:05.880
it himself. Maybe Jedi are simply better&nbsp;
prepared to connect with such a weapon, or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:09.896
maybe they have a built-in connection since they&nbsp;
construct their own lightsabers as younglings.

